0..73 Comment "// A flow between list types by a translator that recurses into the tail,"
74..148 Comment "// after directed univalence (Gratzer, Weinberger and Buchholtz, _Directed"
149..217 Comment "// univalence in simplicial homotopy type theory_, arXiv:2407.09146,"
218..295 Comment "// Definition 1.2): at one cell the image binds the translator\'s own image of"
296..369 Comment "// the rigid tail, and the cell it returns over that image and the head\'s"
370..435 Comment "// leaves is natural, so the translator is natural at every list."
